<%#
  ONE FOLDER OF THE PROJECT LAYOUT (stage 4, S4-2; story 4.3): its name, the extensions that file
  into it as chips, and one add form for the card.

  A CHIP CARRIES ITS EXTENSION AND REMOVE, AND NOTHING ELSE. Moving `.dxf` from design to laser is
  Remove on one card and Add on the other -- two clicks on a rare action, where a folder picker per
  chip would put a select on all 124 of them, and a free-text folder field per chip is what made
  "dsign" a real, silent outcome on the flat page this replaced. Creating a NEW folder is still
  free text, in the add form below, so nothing was taken away.

  Locals: folder (the folder name), by_folder (folder name to its rules, grouped once in #index --
  a `where` here would be a query per card).
%>
<section class="filing-card">
  <h2 class="filing-folder mono"><%= folder %>/</h2>
  <% rules = by_folder[folder] || [] %>
  <ul class="filing-exts">
    <% rules.each do |rule| %>
      <li class="chip filing-chip">
        <span class="mono">.<%= rule.ext %></span>
        <%= button_to "Remove", settings_filing_rule_path(rule), method: :delete,
                      class: "linkbtn danger small",
                      form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Remove the filing rule for .#{rule.ext}? " \
                                                      "It will file into other until you add a new one." } } %>
      </li>
    <% end %>
    <% if rules.empty? %>
      <li class="empty muted">Nothing files here yet.</li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
  <%# scope: :filing_rule names the params at all (this form has no model object), which is what
      Settings::FilingRulesController#create requires -- CLAUDE.md's form-scope rule, asserted on
      the RENDERED field names in settings_filing_test.rb. The folder rides as a hidden field so
      adding an extension to this card is one text box.

      id: nil ON BOTH FIELDS, WHICH THE FLAT PAGE DID NOT NEED. There is one of these forms per
      CARD now, and form_with derives an id from the scope alone -- so the default spelling puts
      eleven elements with id "filing_rule_ext" on one page, which is invalid HTML and hands
      getElementById an arbitrary one of them. The label WRAPS its input, so the association is
      implicit and survives having no id at all; the params are unaffected, which is why the
      rendered-field-name assertions still read the same. %>
  <%= form_with url: settings_filing_rules_path, scope: :filing_rule, class: "settings-add filing-add" do |f| %>
    <%= f.hidden_field :folder, value: folder, id: nil %>
    <label>
      <span>Add extension</span>
      <%= f.text_field :ext, required: true, placeholder: "lbrn", id: nil %>
    </label>
    <%= f.submit "Add", class: "btn ghost small" %>
  <% end %>
</section>
